# A prepared permanent that phases out is not on the battlefield, so the copy of its prepare spell in exile ceases to exist
# (CR 722.3c, 704.5e, 702.26b); as it phases in prepared its controller creates a copy again (CR 722.3c). Blossom-Blessed
# Angel enters prepared on turn 1; on turn 3 Bot1's Teferi's Protection phases it out, and Seed Suture's copy is gone. On
# turn 5 the Angel phases in still prepared, with a new Seed Suture in exile, which Bot1 casts on it.

